<title>UK: Pilkington makes profit warning.</title>
<headline>Pilkington makes profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>British glassmaker Plikington Plc said on Tuesday that profits for the year to March 31, 1997 would be below market estimates, but expected profit before tax and exceptionals to not be less than 130 million stg.</p>
<p>It blamed market conditions in Europe, particularly in Germany, and said that float glass price increases introduced in October had not been sustained and there had been a significant fall in float prices since the end of 1996.</p>
</text>
